Both files are below. The world imports `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0` as the approved grant, and `run` stores its input under `last-input` on every call. The returned batch is built only from the fetch results, so the output is unchanged. I haven't compiled or run it.

The stored value is the subscription URLs joined with newlines. `http-client.fetch` returns transport failures as values, so a dead feed becomes a `FetchFailure` rather than failing the whole run. A URL outside the allowlist still traps at the boundary, which is intended.

